      "body": {
        "name": "JH16 — potwierdzenie",
        "target_id": "jh2016",
        "hypotheses": [
          {
            "id": "H-harm",
            "statement": "Wskaźnik szkodliwości Hi = Ni_harm / Ni × 100% z liczby wyników Google koreluje dodatnio i istotnie z ekspercką oceną szkodliwości Nutt i in. 2010.",
            "tested_by": [
              "harm_index_vs_reference_pearson"
            ],
            "kind": "primary"
          },
          {
            "id": "H-pop",
            "statement": "Liczba wyników Ni daje ranking popularności Pi = Ni / max(Ni) × 100%; publikacja weryfikuje go jakościowo, WatchDog — stabilnością rankingu względem Tabeli 1.",
            "tested_by": [
              "popularity_ranking_stability"
            ],
            "kind": "descriptive"
          }
        ],
        "primary": [
          "harm_index_vs_reference_pearson"
        ],
        "family": [
          {
            "claim_key": "harm_index_vs_reference_pearson",
            "label": "Pearson Hi vs Nutt 2010",
            "hypothesis": "H-harm",
            "p_value": "hi_vs_reference.pearson",
            "claim": {
              "claim_key": "harm_index_vs_reference_pearson",
              "claim_type": "correlation",
              "statistic": "pearson",
              "claimed_value_numeric": 0.8162,
              "unit": "coefficient",
              "tolerance_kind": "interval",
              "tolerance_value": 0.7,
              "interval_upper": 1,
              "notes": "The paper reports 'correlation coefficient between the harm score ranking and the harm index was 81.6%', p=0.000143, alpha=0.01, n=16. The word 'ranking' reads as a rank correlation but is loose: recomputing from the paper's own Tables 1 and 3 gives Pearson r=0.8162 (matching) and Spearman rho=0.5668 (not matching). Registered as Pearson with a floor of 0.70 expressed as the interval [0.70, 1.0]. 0.70 is the conventional strong-correlation threshold, below the published 0.816 to allow drift, and above the ~0.62 needed for significance at n=16 under the authors' own alpha."
            }
          },
          {
            "claim_key": "popularity_ranking_stability",
            "label": "Spearman Pi vs Tabela 1",
            "hypothesis": "H-pop",
            "p_value": "pi_vs_published",
            "claim": {
              "claim_key": "popularity_ranking_stability",
              "claim_type": "rank_correlation",
              "statistic": "spearman",
              "claimed_value_numeric": 1,
              "unit": "coefficient",
              "tolerance_kind": "rank_correlation_floor",
              "tolerance_value": 0.6,
              "notes": "Spearman of the observed Pi ranking against the paper's published Table 1 ranking. Floor anchored in the paper's own data rather than convention: Table 2 gives Pi at six dates over 25 months, and the ranking's Spearman between first and last is 0.785 — how much the authors' own ranking moved against itself in two years. A 2014-to-2026 gap is roughly six times longer, so the floor sits meaningfully below 0.785."
            }
          }
        ],
        "multiplicity": "holm",
        "alpha": 0.01,
        "rationale": "Rodzina: H-harm (główne) i H-pop; Holm, alfa 0,01 jak w publikacji. Zamrożone przed nowym pomiarem 2026-10-26.",
